commit f874533819ac752449e0d07edf32f5519c351000
Author: Wallace Chan <naahtec@hotmail.com>
Date:   Mon Jun 15 12:43:18 2026 -0400

    feat(#12458): guard the reboot decision with the pause-aware check (AC3/AC5)
    
    The sensitive core of slice c. update_health's auto-reboot path now HOLDS
    instead of rebooting a dead-PID agent while a hook explains the silence,
    mirroring the proven crash-looping hold/resume pattern so the status-machine
    one-shot (was_alive) is handled correctly.
    
    - death_candidate = a fresh death OR a still-dead "paused" agent. If
      active_pause(now) is set (in-flight/compacting/waiting, each ceiling-bounded)
      → status="paused" (preserved across polls by the status block, which now
      also preserves "paused"), no reboot. Re-evaluated every poll; released the
      moment the ceiling elapses → normal death path runs (AC4).
    - AC3d: a death coinciding with a recent rate_limit/overloaded StopFailure
      backs off via the crash-loop timer (counts as a fast death so repeated
      throttles escalate) instead of re-hitting the limit — reuses the
      crash-looping resume path.
    - AC5: a genuine death with NO pause signal is untouched (active_pause→None
      immediately) — verified by test_genuine_death_no_pause_reboots plus the full
      #12244 crash-loop suite staying green.
    - Operator stop still wins over a hold (the "paused" status settles to stopped
      under STOPPING intent).
    
    Refactor: the kept #12244 backoff block moved from `else:` under the old `if`
    to `elif death_candidate:` (dedented to match) — logic byte-identical, only
    the guard wraps it. TestPauseGuard12458 (10 tests); full harness suite green
    (266).
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

